course: dictionary
lesson: 16140
title: Widening: wider, and growing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Widening means becoming wider, or making something wider. It comes from the word wide. «The council is widening the road to stop traffic jams.» The road is getting wider, so widening means making it wider.
explain: The word can also describe a problem that is growing. «There is a widening gap between the fastest and slowest runners.» A gap is not a road, so it cannot get wider in the same way. Ask yourself: is the gap getting bigger? If it is, widening means growing.
explain: Widening is part of the verb widen, which changes to widens, widened and widening. It can also work as a noun or an adjective. «Her eyes widened in surprise» uses the verb in the past tense, and the same word family shows the change: the eyes are getting bigger and rounder.
fact: Widen is the verb. Widening is its -ing form, and it can also be a noun or an adjective.
fact: «Widening» means becoming wider, or making something wider.
fact: A widening gap or problem is one that is getting bigger.
fact: «Her eyes widened» means her eyes opened wider, often because she was surprised.
fact: Phrases you may meet are road widening, widening gap and eyes widening.
exercise: «The workers are widening the road near our school.» What does widening mean here? | Painting the road white | Making the road shorter | *Making the road wider | Closing the road for ever
exercise: «There is a widening gap between the fastest and slowest runners.» What is getting bigger? | The race | The finish line | *The gap | The runners
exercise: «Her eyes widened when she saw the birthday cake.» Find and copy one word that is a form of widen. | *widened | saw | eyes | cake
test: «The river was widening as the rain fell all night.» Which word tells you the river was getting wider? | *widening | night | river | rain
test: Ben says a widening gap means a gap that is getting smaller. Is he right? | Yes, it means the gap is getting smaller | No, it is a kind of bridge | *No, a widening gap is getting bigger | Yes, the gap has closed
exam: «The council announced road widening work, and the widening gap between the towns worried many families.» Which meaning fits a widening gap? | Shrinking to nothing | Being filled in | Becoming smaller | *Getting bigger
